# Root .dockerignore — keeps the build context lean.
#
# This file governs EVERY build whose context is the repository root: the API
# image built from the root Dockerfile, and the dashboard built from
# Dockerfile.web. Dokku always uses the repository root as the build context, so
# these patterns are what decide what the daemon receives.
#
# Patterns are matched against paths RELATIVE TO THE CONTEXT ROOT, so a bare
# `node_modules/` excludes only the root one — `frontend/node_modules` needs the
# `**/` form. That distinction matters here because the dashboard's dependencies
# are 1.3 GB.
**/node_modules/
**/.next/
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.turbo/
**/.swc/
**/*.tsbuildinfo

.env*
!.env.example
!.env.production.example
!.env.local.example
.git/
.gitignore
.graphify-out/
graphify-out/
backend/pocketbase/pb_data/
backend/pocketbase/pocketbase
*.md
!.README.md
.DS_Store
.claude/
.agents/
.hallmark/
.zcode/
.v2c/

# NOTE: `frontend/` used to be excluded here. It was removed because Dokku builds
# every app with the repository root as its context, so excluding it made a
# root-context dashboard build impossible — `COPY frontend/package.json` would
# simply not find the file. The API image is unaffected: its Dockerfile copies
# only backend/ paths, so the extra frontend/ sources are transferred and ignored.
